<title>HONG KONG: World Bank launches HK$1.0 bln fixed rate bond.</title>
<headline>World Bank launches HK$1.0 bln fixed rate bond.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue was announced by lead manager HSBC Markets.</p>
<p> BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p> AMT   HK$1.0 BLN    COUPON     7.58 PCT   MATURITY   07.MAY.07</p>
<p> TYPE  FIXED BOND    SPREAD     33 BP	PAY DATE   07.MAY.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY AAA	ISS PRICE  PAR	  LAUNCH     07.APR.97</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   AAA	REOFFER    PAR	  FULL FEES  32.5 BP</p>
<p> MGT/UND    NA	 SELL CONC  NA	   PAY FREQ   QUARTERLY</p>
<p> LISTING    HK	 HOME CTRY  SUPRA	CLEARING   CMU</p>
<p> NOTES -    *PRICED TO YIELD 33 BASIS POINTS OVER THE JANUARY</p>
<p>		2007 HONG KONG EXCHANGE FUND NOTE**</p>
<p>		**ISSUED OFF THE WORLD BANK'S GLOBAL DEBT ISSUANCE</p>
<p>		PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>		***ISSUER HAS APPLIED TO THE HKMA TO ACCEPT THE</p>
<p>		BONDS AS ELIGIBLE FOR USE AT ITS LIQUIDITY</p>
<p>		ADJUSTMENT FACILITY (LAF), OR DISCOUNT WINDOW.</p>
<p>		A GROUP IS BEING FORMED.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
</text>
